A||||4||GT Bastard||My pre-Fiero rides....  pics||||12||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||05-26-2000||01:04 AM||||Here's my favorite f-body.  It was my 3rd Camaro, and I was 17 when I got it.  I named her Blackie (for obvious reasons.)  She was a sweetheart.  305 V8 H.O., 3.73 gears, auto, t-tops, all power options.... And only 59,000 origional miles when I got her.  I wish I still had it.  That car was a wicked performer.  It still holds my record burnout of 37ft on NEW p215 60R 15's.  It was in the back of a Walmart parking lot, and I was so proud that I paced it off!  anyhow...  Her tranny blew while cruizing down the highway(it always had problems.)  I ended up accepting an offer I couldn't refuse.  Still regretting it.   <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Blackie1.jpg"> <P>Here's my first car... 1984 Base model coupe. V6, F41 suspension, NO other cool options.  This car was a hand-me-down, and it was a dog, but everybody thought it looked fast. Note the pimpin' paint job my dad gave it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pimp1.jpg"> <P>Last but not least, my '85 IROC... When my dad got this car, it didn't run.  It had sand in the gas tank, and no exhaust! It had a TPI 305, and it had a rough life... Note the "meat is murder" sticker in the back window.  I used to be very hardcore vegetarian in HS.  My dad passed this car on to me when I was 16.  Needless to say, it had bald tires and all the usual wear of an idiot driver.  THIS car hold the record for the most air-time of any car I've owned, but that's a story for another day.  You may find it hard to believe, but I baby my Fiero! Still miss some of these cars though.<BR>Anyhow... later guys<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Iroc1.jpg"> ||||reg||12
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||05-26-2000||09:56 PM||||I had an 84 Camaro Berlinetta with the 305. It ran OK, but I was doing lots of work to it. I replaced the dirty,ugly interior with the interior from a wrecked 89 Firebird (this was in 1989 when I was 17) and got some 16" I-ROC wheels for it. It was looking good til some guy backed into it and crushed the rear quarter panel... then the engine let go and I kinda let it sit. I bought an 86SE Fiero from my brother and let the Camaro go for almost nothing. I miss that car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||05-26-2000||10:13 PM||||You want pre Fiero, I don't think you can handle this pre Fiero!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/47Chevy.jpg"> <P>Egad, I had dark hair.   ||||reg||5
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||05-27-2000||12:19 AM||||I didn't know there was a Mcdonald's around in 1886  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. Look at that old guy struggling to lift that hood... he must be pushing 60 in that picture... wonder if he is still around.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Just kidding... what year was that taken?||||reg||12
Z||000004||Old Lar||05-27-2000||10:17 AM||||Not only is the old guy around, the car is still around.  The McDonalds is gone.<P>I think the photo is from 1977.<P>This was my first project car.||||reg||1
